# What does "ownership" mean? This team is the **first contact** when it comes to anything regarding this package. For
# example, technical, design, behavioral and functional changes and questions.

# What does "ownership" NOT mean?
# Ownership does NOT mean that the owner-team is the only team that may change code in this package. But you should
# consult the owner-team if you plan more significant changes. Ownership does NOT mean that the owner-team is the only
# team responsible for the package's stability and functioning. We are all responsible for a stable and working Instana.
# But if anything breaks, then the owner-team is the best place to start looking for help. Ownership does NOT mean that
# the owner-team has ownership over all the code within a package. It might well be that a component serves different
# purposes (and teams). But if in doubt, the owner-team at least knows whom to ask for advice, i.e., which other team or
# person.

